{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>These are the generations of Jacob.</b> The events that befell him and what came upon him after he settled there. For from the time he left his father's house, his affairs were like what happened to our fathers in the first exile, and from the time he returned to the land of his father's sojourning, what befell him was like what happened to our fathers in the Second Temple — its destruction, its exile, and its redemption at the end of days (Proverbs 27:1)." "<b>He was shepherding his brothers with the flock.</b> He was guiding and instructing them in the work of tending the flock." "<b>And he was a youth.</b> Because of his youth he sinned in bringing an evil report of his brothers, for he did not weigh or reflect on the outcome of a matter — even though he was then exceedingly discerning, and though afterward he instructed the elders of the generation, as it says: וְזְקֵנָיו יְחַכֵּם (Psalms 105:22). And this is as they said, of blessed memory (Shabbat 89a): וְלֹא בְּדַרְדְּקֵי עֵצָה." "<b>And Joseph brought an evil report of them.</b> In telling his father that his brothers were erring and causing loss, without proper understanding, in the work of livestock — which was then the main focus of their effort in acquiring wealth and property."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {0 "The citation of Proverbs 27:1 at the end is textually unexpected for its content; included as it appears in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:34.772904755Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}